{"tool_name":"msms","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"msms","identifiers":["biotools:msms","doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btq322"],"license":"Not available","summary":"Msms is a program written in the c programming language to compute molecular surfaces.","home_url":"http://mgltools.scripps.edu/packages/MSMS/","keywords":["Computer Simulation","Demography","Genetic Loci","Humans","Population","Recombination, Genetic","Selection, Genetic","Population genetics","Systems biology"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":0},"biotools":{"id":"msms","home":"http://www.mabs.at/ewing/msms/index.shtml","license":"LGPL-3.0","summary":"MSMS is a coalescent simulator that and permits the full range of demographic models provided by ms, in particular, it allows for multiple demes with arbitrary migration patterns, population growth and decay, and for population splits and merges. Applications include power studies, analytical comparisons, approximated Bayesian computation among others.","addition_date":"2017-08-20T15:58:15Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:05:18.152318Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"collections":["Animal and Crop Genomics"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:msms","credit":[{"email":"gregory.ewine@univie.ac.at","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://www.mabs.at/ewing/msms/manual.shtml"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["animalandcropgenomics"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Modelling and simulation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2426"}]}],"name":"msms","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"admin","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btq322","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: We have implemented a coalescent simulation program for a structured population with selection at a single diploid locus. The program includes the functionality of the simulator ms to model population structure and 